---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the journal"
  description="Fieldnotes is an independent journal about software engineering, deliberate decisions, and the people behind the code."
>
  <div class="shell page-content">
    <div class="about-content">
      <header class="page-intro">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> A note about this journal
        </div>
        <h1>
          For people who care
          <br />
          about the craft.
        </h1>
        <p>Software is a technical pursuit. Building it well is a human one.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Fieldnotes is an independent engineering journal for people who like
          to look a little closer. At the decisions behind a system. At the
          tradeoffs behind a tool. At the habits that make a team a good place
          to do good work.
        </p>
        <p>
          We believe the most useful engineering writing begins with a real
          question and makes room for an honest answer. Sometimes that answer is
          a code example. Sometimes it is a diagram. Often, it is a better
          question.
        </p>
        <div class="about-callout">
          Less noise. More signal.
          <br />A little perspective on the things we build.
        </div>
        <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
        <p>
          Practical essays on architecture, development, performance, and
          engineering culture. We share the reasoning alongside the result, so
          you can decide what fits your own context.
        </p>
        <h2>A small editorial promise</h2>
        <p>
          Clear explanations. Specific examples. Respect for your time. No
          manufactured urgency, and no assumption that the newest tool is the
          right one.
        </p>
        <h2>Meet the contributors</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Maya Chen</strong> writes about software architecture and
          finding the right boundaries. <strong>Alex Rivera</strong> explores
          TypeScript and testing. <strong>Sam Okafor</strong> focuses on web
          performance and the experience on the other side of the screen.{" "}
          <strong>Jordan Lee</strong> writes about collaboration and
          maintainable code.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is a sample publication. Its contributors and editorial identity
          are fictional; the engineering lessons are here to be used.
        </p>
        <h2>Keep a thread open</h2>
        <p>
          Every article is available in our <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>. Add
          it to your favorite reader and new notes will find their way to you.
          No account or inbox required.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a href="/" class="button-link">
        Back to the journal <Icon name="arrow" size={17} />
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
